{
 "id": "ll_harvest",
 "title": "Greyhold Harvest",
 "kind": "hero",
 "seed": 4101,
 "intro": [
  "Harvest in the southern marches, and the barrow fields are moving. Shamblers have dug themselves out of the old graves east of Greyhold and made a camp in the fen. Sir Aldous Wren, the town's lord, has no army to send. He walks out through his own fields to see for himself.",
  "How to play: right click to walk and fight. Right click a villager to talk; a gold ! means they want something from you, a ? means you can report back. Your quests are listed on the left. Q, W, E and R use Aldous's skills, K opens his skill trees when he gains a level. If he falls he wakes at the last shrine he touched, a little poorer.",
  "Find Reeve Hamlin Dace at Hobb's Acre. The dead here will not come to you. Take your time."
 ],
 "outro": [
  {
   "if": {
    "flag": "grue_spared"
   },
   "text": [
    "The barrow camp burns. The dead it held were fresh: farmers buried this summer, and others that no one in Greyhold remembers burying at all. The ground in the barrow fields is warm to the touch.",
    "Sexton Grue is gone from his fields. A carter saw a lantern going south along the old roads, and the dead walking behind it in good order."
   ]
  },
  {
   "if": {
    "flag": "grue_chained"
   },
   "text": [
    "The barrow camp burns. The dead it held were fresh: farmers buried this summer, and others that no one in Greyhold remembers burying at all. The ground in the barrow fields is warm to the touch.",
    "The cart that carried Sexton Grue reached Greyhold empty. His chains were unlocked, not broken."
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": [
    "The barrow camp burns. The dead it held were fresh: farmers buried this summer, and others that no one in Greyhold remembers burying at all. The ground in the barrow fields is warm to the touch.",
    "They buried Sexton Grue at the edge of his own barrow field. By morning the grave stood open."
   ]
  }
