 "dialogues": {
  "reeve_first": {
   "nodes": {
    "start": {
     "text": "My lord! You came yourself. There's no one else, is there. The levy went east in spring and never wrote.",
     "next": "b"
    },
    "b": {
     "who": "hero",
     "text": "Tell me what's happening in my fields, Hamlin.",
     "next": "c"
    },
    "c": {
     "text": "Rats first, a plague of them in the barley, bold as dogs. They came up out of the ground by the barrows. And behind the rats, my lord... the dead. Walking. Folk we buried this summer.",
     "choices": [
      {
       "text": "I'll clear the rats. Then we'll talk about the dead.",
       "do": [
        {
         "flag": "met_reeve"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "text": "The dead first. Where are they?",
       "next": "d"
      }
     ]
    },
    "d": {
     "text": "East, past the barrow fields, in the fen. But you'll not get there through rats, my lord. Clear the grain, and I'll show you their tracks.",
     "do": [
      {
       "flag": "met_reeve"
      }
     ]
    }
   }
  },
  "reeve_rats": {
   "nodes": {
    "start": {
     "text": "The barley's clear. Bless you, my lord. Now look here: the tracks. Bare feet, in rows, going east to the barrow fields. Walking like soldiers.",
     "next": "b"
    },
    "b": {
     "text": "And there's one more thing I'm ashamed to say. Men in levy coats took Holt's Mill a week ago, and the grain with it. Greyhold men. Ours.",
     "choices": [
      {
       "text": "I'll go to the mill.",
       "do": [
        {
         "flag": "reeve_rats"
        },
        {
         "start_quest": "mill"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "text": "The dead come first. The mill can wait.",
       "do": [
        {
         "flag": "reeve_rats"
        },
        {
         "start_quest": "mill"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    }
   }
  },
  "reeve_mill_hanged": {
   "nodes": {
    "start": {
     "text": "Hanged? Well. That's the law, and they knew it. The grain will feed the village till spring. Here, my lord, the mill's tithe. It's yours by right.",
     "do": [
      {
       "flag": "reeve_mill"
      },
      {
       "marks": 150
      }
     ]
    }
   }
  },
  "reeve_mill_joined": {
   "nodes": {
    "start": {
     "text": "You took them in? Men who ran? I'll say nothing, my lord, but the village will. Here's what tithe there is.",
     "do": [
      {
       "flag": "reeve_mill"
      },
      {
       "marks": 50
      }
     ]
    }
   }
  },
  "reeve_mill_freed": {
   "nodes": {
    "start": {
     "text": "Gone, and the grain left behind? That's more mercy than they earned, my lord, but I'll take the grain. Here's the mill's tithe.",
     "do": [
      {
       "flag": "reeve_mill"
      },
      {
       "marks": 100
      }
     ]
    }
   }
  },
  "reeve_idle": {
   "nodes": {
    "start": {
     "text": "The barrow fields are east, my lord. Mind the fen; the ground there's warm, they say. Warm in autumn."
    }
   }
  },
  "marta_ask": {
   "nodes": {
    "start": {
     "text": "My lord, please. My Tobin went into the Fellwood for herbs two days ago. The wolves have been bold since the sky went strange. He's only twelve.",
     "choices": [
      {
       "text": "I'll find him.",
       "do": [
        {
         "start_quest": "boy"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "text": "I have the dead to deal with. Later.",
       "next": "b"
      }
     ]
    },
    "b": {
     "text": "Later. Yes, my lord. Everyone says later."
    }
   }
  },
  "marta_back": {
   "nodes": {
    "start": {
     "text": "He's home! He came in muddy and grinning like nothing happened. Thank you, my lord. Thank you.",
     "do": [
      {
       "flag": "marta_told"
      }
     ]
    }
   }
  },
  "marta_back_silver": {
   "nodes": {
    "start": {
     "text": "He's home! He came in muddy and grinning like nothing happened. Thank you, my lord. Thank you.",
     "next": "b"
    },
    "b": {
     "text": "And the silver he brought... it will see us through the winter. Take these, they were my husband's. He won't need them now.",
     "do": [
      {
       "flag": "marta_told"
      }
     ]
    }
   }
  },
  "marta_idle": {
   "nodes": {
    "start": {
     "text": "Tobin's out in the yard chopping wood. First time he's done it without being told."
    }
   }
  },
  "tobin_wolves": {
   "nodes": {
    "start": {
     "text": "There's wolves at the den, my lord! Big ones! I'm staying up here."
    }
   }
  },
  "tobin_idle": {
   "nodes": {
    "start": {
     "text": "I'm going home now. Don't tell Mum I was scared."
    }
   }
  },
  "tobin_found": {
   "nodes": {
    "start": {
     "text": "You killed them all! Look what I found in the den, my lord. A dead knight's bones and this, all silver, with a saint on it.",
     "next": "b"
    },
    "b": {
     "text": "It's worth something, isn't it? Mum says we'll be short this winter, with the harvest half eaten.",
     "choices": [
      {
       "text": "Take it home to your mother. It will feed you both.",
       "do": [
        {
         "flag": "helped_marta"
        },
        {
         "flag": "tobin_decided"
        },
        {
         "leave": "tobin",
         "to": "hobbs_acre"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "text": "A knight's relic belongs with a knight. I'll keep it.",
       "do": [
        {
         "flag": "reliquary_kept"
        },
        {
         "flag": "tobin_decided"
        },
        {
         "leave": "tobin",
         "to": "hobbs_acre"
        }
       ],
       "next": "c"
      }
     ]
    },
    "c": {
     "text": "Oh. Yes, my lord. Of course, my lord."
    }
   }
  },
  "bram": {
   "nodes": {
    "start": {
     "who": "bram",
     "text": "That's far enough, my lord. Yes, I know you. I stood in your levy at the spring muster.",
     "next": "b"
    },
    "b": {
     "who": "hero",
     "text": "Then you know what happens to deserters, Bram Holt.",
     "next": "c"
    },
    "c": {
     "text": "We didn't run from the war. Captain sent us to the barrow fields to dig the dead back in. The dead dug us out instead. Half the company. We ran, we ate, we took the grain. I'll not say sorry for living.",
     "choices": [
      {
       "text": "Then live under my banner. The dead are where I'm going.",
       "do": [
        {
         "flag": "bram_decided"
        },
        {
         "flag": "deserters_joined"
        },
        {
         "join": "deserters"
        },
        {
         "join": "bram"
        }
       ],
       "next": "join"
      },
      {
       "text": "Leave the grain and go. If I see you again, you hang.",
       "do": [
        {
         "flag": "bram_decided"
        },
        {
         "flag": "deserters_freed"
        },
        {
         "leave": "deserters",
         "to": [
          0.03,
          0.08
         ]
        },
        {
         "leave": "bram",
         "to": [
          0.03,
          0.08
         ]
        }
       ],
       "next": "free"
      },
      {
       "text": "The law is the law. Draw steel.",
       "do": [
        {
         "flag": "bram_decided"
        },
        {
         "flag": "deserters_hanged"
        },
        {
         "hostile": "deserters"
        },
        {
         "hostile": "bram"
        },
        {
         "say": "Then come and take us, my lord!",
         "who": "bram"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    "join": {
     "text": "...Aye, my lord. We'll follow. Better your banner than their teeth."
    },
    "free": {
     "text": "You're a fair man, my lord. Fairer than the captain. We'll not trouble Greyhold again."
    }
   }
  },
  "bram_after": {
   "nodes": {
    "start": {
     "text": "Where you lead, my lord."
    }
   }
  },
  "anselm_ask": {
   "nodes": {
    "start": {
     "text": "My lord Wren. Cutthroats have taken the old bell tower by my chapel. They ring the bell at dusk, and travellers come to see who is in need. Nobody comes back. I cannot ring for the dead while they hold it.",
     "choices": [
      {
       "text": "I'll clear the tower.",
       "do": [
        {
         "start_quest": "bell"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "text": "Not now, brother."
      }
     ]
    }
   }
  },
  "anselm_back": {
   "nodes": {
    "start": {
     "text": "I heard the bell from here, on its own, when the last of them fell. Kneel at my shrine whenever you pass, my lord. The saint keeps her own.",
     "do": [
      {
       "flag": "anselm_done"
      }
     ]
    }
   }
  },
  "anselm_idle": {
   "nodes": {
    "start": {
     "text": "The saint keeps her own, my lord. Even now."
    }
   }
  },
  "wenna": {
   "nodes": {
    "start": {
     "text": "Don't... don't strike. I'm Wenna. Wenna from the Acre. I only want to go home.",
     "next": "b"
    },
    "b": {
     "who": "hero",
     "text": "Your home is a grave, Wenna.",
     "next": "c"
    },
    "c": {
     "text": "Yes. That's the one. It was cool there. Now it's hot, so hot, and everyone's walking. I want to lie down again.",
     "choices": [
      {
       "text": "Then go, and rest.",
       "do": [
        {
         "flag": "wenna_decided"
        },
        {
         "flag": "mercy_to_the_dead"
        },
        {
         "leave": "wenna",
         "to": "open_graves"
        }
       ],
       "next": "go"
      },
      {
       "text": "I'm sorry, Wenna. I'll put you to rest myself.",
       "do": [
        {
         "flag": "wenna_decided"
        },
        {
         "flag": "wenna_fight"
        },
        {
         "hostile": "wenna"
        },
        {
         "spawn": "wenna_kin"
        },
        {
         "attack": "wenna_kin",
         "to": "hero"
        },
        {
         "say": "No... no...",
         "who": "wenna"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    "go": {
     "text": "Thank you, my lord. You're a kind boy. You always were."
    }
   }
  },
  "grue": {
   "nodes": {
    "start": {
     "text": "Mind the edges, my lord, they crumble. I'm Grue, the sexton. I've buried Greyhold's dead for thirty years. These are my neighbours.",
     "next": "b"
    },
    "b": {
     "who": "hero",
     "text": "Your neighbours are walking into my fen, sexton.",
     "next": "c"
    },
    "c": {
     "text": "The ground's too hot for them. Something underneath. They come to me because I'm the one who put them down, and I'm the only one who'll talk to them. Someone ought to keep them in good order.",
     "choices": [
      {
       "text": "Then keep them. Away from my villages.",
       "do": [
        {
         "flag": "grue_decided"
        },
        {
         "flag": "grue_spared"
        },
        {
         "leave": "grue",
         "to": [
          0.98,
          0.92
         ]
        }
       ],
       "next": "spare"
      },
      {
       "text": "You're coming to Greyhold in chains. The abbess will want to hear this.",
       "do": [
        {
         "flag": "grue_decided"
        },
        {
         "flag": "grue_chained"
        },
        {
         "leave": "grue",
         "to": "greyhold"
        }
       ],
       "next": "chain"
      },
      {
       "text": "You command the dead. That ends here.",
       "do": [
        {
         "flag": "grue_decided"
        },
        {
         "flag": "grue_fight"
        },
        {
         "hostile": "grue"
        },
        {
         "spawn": "grue_dead"
        },
        {
         "attack": "grue_dead",
         "to": "hero"
        },
        {
         "say": "Up, neighbours. Up!",
         "who": "grue"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    "spare": {
     "text": "Thank you, my lord. I'll take them south, where it's cool. Mind the camp in the fen. Those ones aren't mine."
    },
    "chain": {
     "text": "As you like, my lord. I'll walk. The dead don't need me to hold their hands any more."
    }
   }
  },
  "maelis_meet": {
   "nodes": {
    "start": {
     "text": "My lord. I wondered when you'd come. I've been in the reeds two days, counting them.",
     "next": "b"
